<%#
  Wallet brand-icon sprite — inline brand marks for the wallets the Connect-Wallet
  picker knows about (Phantom, Solflare, Backpack), OWNED BY THE ENGINE so every
  consumer inherits crisp brand icons with ZERO per-app asset files. Before this,
  the picker referenced app-served PNGs (/wallet-phantom.png, ...), so a fresh app
  that had not copied those into its own public/ showed 404 letter tiles (P/S/B).

  Render this ONCE inside a picker's single root, then reference a mark by name:

    <svg class="w-9 h-9"><use href="#se-wallet-phantom"></use></svg>

  or, in an Alpine x-for over detected wallets, resolve the id from the name:

    <use :href="'#se-wallet-' + brandIcon(w.name)"></use>   (brandIcon() lowercases
    the name and returns it only for a known brand, else null → letter fallback).

  The sprite is visually hidden (zero-box, absolute) and aria-hidden; only the
  <use> references paint. Each <symbol> carries the OFFICIAL brand asset embedded
  inline as a base64 PNG data-URI <image> — byte-identical to the real logos each
  wallet ships (matching Turf Monster's public/wallet-*.png), so no hand-drawn
  approximation drifts from the brand. The letter tile stays the fallback for any
  wallet not in this set.
%>
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
     style="position:absolute;width:0;height:0;overflow:hidden" data-wallet-brand-sprite>
  <%# Phantom — official brand mark (light-purple tile, cream ghost). %>
  <symbol id="se-wallet-phantom" viewBox="0 0 460 460">
    <image width="460" height="460" href="data:image/png;base64,"/>
  </symbol>

  <%# Solflare — official brand mark (yellow tile, black blackletter S). %>
  <symbol id="se-wallet-solflare" viewBox="0 0 361 361">
    <image width="361" height="361" href="data:image/png;base64,"/>
  </symbol>

  <%# Backpack — official brand mark (red tile, white pack). %>
  <symbol id="se-wallet-backpack" viewBox="0 0 128 128">
    <image width="128" height="128" href="data:image/png;base64,"/>
  </symbol>
</svg>
